issue_context.body:
Currently the `knn` section in the search request only accepts one field. We should extend it to allow ANN search over multiple fields:

```
POST image-index/_search
{
  "knn": [{
    "field": "image-vector",
    "query_vector": [-5, 9, -12],
    "k": 10,
    "num_candidates": 50
  }, {
    "field": "caption-vector",
    "query_vector": [0.91, -0.21, 0.43],
    "k": 10,
    "num_candidates": 100
  }],
  "fields": [ "title", "file-type" ]
}
```

Each section would be combined like a disjunction (the same as we do when both `knn` and `query` are specified). Note that it's already possible for documents to have more than one `dense_vector` field. It's just not currently possible to search them in the same request.

comments:
field such as `query_vector` could get very lengthy , but other than that - it might be useful if we can allow syntax for same vector to multiple fields , allowing multiple boosts . sort of like `multi_match`

```
{
  "knn": {
    "field": ["text-vector","description-vector"],
    "query_vector": [0.91, -0.21, 0.43],
    "k": 10,
    "num_candidates":50
    "boost": [1, 2.0]
  },
  "fields": [ "title", "file-type" ]
}
```

or 

```
{
  "knn": {
    "field": ["text-vector^10","description-vector^12"],
    "query_vector": [0.91, -0.21, 0.43],
    "k": 10,
    "num_candidates":50
  },
  "fields": [ "title", "file-type" ]
}

```
